  "details": "<p>The archive is located in a private house in Assur.</p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"767\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan62_AssurPlan.png\" width=\"560\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In the northern corner, along the northwest town wall of Assur (bD5I, bC/D5II, bC5III), researchers unearthed Houses 67\u201368 with an archive belonging to a family with the title \u1e2bunduraya, a gentilic meaning \"from \u1e2aundur\". Another archive belonging to a related family of \u1e2bunduraya was found nearby (Assur Archive 24). In House 67 and 68, about 48 clay tablets and fragments were found. The tablets mostly date to the second half of the 7th century BC. The archive consists of loans, mostly concerning silver, work contracts, purchase documents and a juridical settlement.",
